+// PICO_CONFIG: PICO_MULTICORE_LOCKOUT_DISABLE_INTERRUPTS, Disable interrupts on the victim core while it is locked out. Setting this to 0 allows higher priority interrupts to continue running on the victim core, which is only safe if their handlers do not access flash or anything else the lockout is protecting, type=bool, default=1, group=pico_multicore
+#ifndef PICO_MULTICORE_LOCKOUT_DISABLE_INTERRUPTS
+#define PICO_MULTICORE_LOCKOUT_DISABLE_INTERRUPTS 1
